This notebook cleans the charted data and checks it against the codebook. The charting form has two tables. data/raw/included_sources_raw.csv has one row per included source. data/raw/included_factors_raw.csv has one row per factor that a source reports. The notebook writes data/processed/included_sources_clean.csv, data/processed/included_factors_clean.csv, and data/processed/bibliography.csv, which holds the reference details of each included source, taken from the deduplicated records.
The variables, the closed value lists, and the required variables are read from codebook.yml, so this notebook holds no copy of them. Cleaning trims whitespace and lowercases the closed variables.
The checks come first. If any check finds an error, the notebook stops and writes nothing. A warning is printed and does not stop the run. Errors are an empty required cell, a value outside the codebook, a repeated source_id, a factor whose source_id is not in the sources table, a record_id that is not in the deduplicated records, and a source_id that screening did not include. Warnings are sources with no factors, included sources not charted yet, repeated factor rows, and factors not yet coded to a category or level.
